  "notes": "Norfolk Island Central School, the island's only school, teaches Prep to Year 12. It joined the Queensland Department of Education on 1 January 2022, ending over a century with NSW; the last NSW HSC cohort finished in 2023. It follows Queensland: Prep (age 5 by 30 June) is the first school year, primary is Prep–Year 6 and secondary Years 7–12, with Years 11–12 on QCAA senior subjects. The part-time Kindergarten year before Prep is left out. Learners schooled under NSW may call Prep 'Kindergarten'."
